<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<Description>Norse.AuthN.Components.FluentUI: Login/LoginWithPasskey/Register Razor components, SignInMethodLinks (every sign-in link the server's URL), plus the FluentUI presentational components migrated off Himinbjorg: ShowRecoveryCodes, ForgotPassword, ResendEmailConfirmation, and the routable shims over plain-parameter units LoginWith2fa/TwoFactorForm, LoginWithRecoveryCode/RecoveryCodeForm, ResetPassword/ResetPasswordForm, ConfirmEmail/ConfirmEmailPanel and ConfirmEmailChange/ConfirmEmailChangePanel (click-to-confirm), and the account-management tree: ManageLayout/ManageNavMenu plus the Manage/ loader-over-form pages Index/ProfileForm, Email/ChangeEmailForm, ChangePassword and SetPassword over the shared PasswordPanel (ChangePasswordForm or SetPasswordForm by HasPassword), DeletePersonalData/DeletePersonalDataForm, ExternalLogins and the moved PersonalData, and the two-factor and passkey pages TwoFactorAuthentication, EnableAuthenticator/VerifyAuthenticatorForm, RecoveryCodesHandoff, ResetAuthenticator, Disable2fa, GenerateRecoveryCodes (click-to-confirm), Passkeys and RenamePasskey/RenamePasskeyForm (passkey ceremonies through wwwroot/passkeys.js), every one stamped by Manage/_Imports.razor with @layout ManageLayout and the Account authorization policy (a reflection lock enforces the stamp), FluentUI Blazor v5, wired to inject IAuthenticationService/IIdentityService/IAccountService/ITwoFactorService/IPasskeyService/ISignInMethodsService directly (transport-dumb; each host registers its own implementation via DI), never a caught exception (spec §9.6/§9.8). Logout.razor lives in the headless AuthN.Components instead — it has no FluentUI markup, only @code.</Description>
		<NorseFrontendPlatforms>All</NorseFrontendPlatforms>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.FluentUI.AspNetCore.Components" Version="5.*" />
		<ProjectReference Include="../AuthN.Components/AuthN.Components.csproj" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
